3. External services called at runtime
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

All of these are network calls made by the running application. Nothing is
bundled; nothing is cached into this repository.

| Service | Endpoint in source | Terms |
|---------|--------------------|-------|
| RCSB Protein Data Bank | `https://files.rcsb.org/download/<id>.pdb` (`src/modules/docking/ReceptorPrep.cpp:420`) | PDB data are released without restriction into the public domain; RCSB asks that the entry and the primary citation be cited |
| AutoDock Vina 1.2.5 (binary provisioning) | `https://github.com/ccsb-scripps/AutoDock-Vina/releases/download/v1.2.5/vina_1.2.5_win.exe` (`src/modules/docking/EngineLocator.cpp:45`) | Apache-2.0 (Trott & Olson 2010, J Comput Chem 31:455-461). Downloaded to the user's app-data directory at runtime; not redistributed by BioCAD |
| Vina-GPU (OpenCL) | `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeltaGroupNJUPT/Vina-GPU/main/` (`src/modules/docking/EngineLocator.cpp:71`) | A derivative of AutoDock Vina; consult the upstream repository for its exact licence before redistributing. BioCAD fetches the prebuilt binaries and the OpenCL kernel at runtime into the user's app-data directory and redistributes nothing |
| smina | located on PATH or in `runtime/engines`; never downloaded (`EngineLocator.cpp:57`) | GPL-2.0. BioCAD only *executes* a smina binary the user supplies; it neither links nor ships it, so no GPL obligation attaches to BioCAD |
| Anthropic Messages API | `https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages` (`src/agent/AnthropicProvider.cpp`) | Anthropic commercial API terms; requires the user's own API key, stored locally via DPAPI |
| DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint | `https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=` (`src/agent/WebTools.cpp:338`) | Used under DuckDuckGo's terms of use; agent `web_search` tool only, `science` feature only |
| DigiCert timestamp authority | `http://timestamp.digicert.com` (`scripts/sign.ps1:37`) | Release-signing infrastructure only; not used by the application |

4. Data sources cited by the shipped packs (`assets/packs/*.json`)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The packs contain BioCAD-authored records. Where a record carries a cross
reference or follows a published selection, the source is named here.

| Source | Where | Terms |
|--------|-------|-------|
| Bowes et al. 2012, "Reducing safety-related drug attrition", Nat Rev Drug Discov 11:909-922 (PMID 23197038) | target selection rationale of `safety-offtarget.json` | Cited work; no text or table is reproduced |
| Eurofins SafetyScreen44 datasheet | the enumerated 44-member panel membership in `safety-offtarget.json` | Eurofins proprietary document, cited as the source of the panel's membership only. The target identifiers themselves are factual protein names |
| ChEMBL identifiers (`xrefs.chembl`) | all four packs (59 records) | ChEMBL data are CC BY-SA 3.0. Only accession strings are stored; **if ChEMBL-derived values are ever added to a pack, that pack inherits the share-alike obligation and must carry the ChEMBL attribution** |
| UniProt accessions (`xrefs.uniprot`) | all four packs (56 records) | UniProt content is CC BY 4.0; attribution required for any UniProt-derived content |
| PubChem CIDs (`xrefs.pubchemCid`) and InChIKeys | `cns-monoamine.json`, `analgesics-otc.json`, `metabolic-and-nutrition.json` | PubChem is US-government public domain; InChI/InChIKey is an IUPAC open standard |
| RCSB PDB entry identifiers and binding-box centres | `targets[].pdb` in all packs | PDB entries are public domain; cite the entry and its primary citation when reporting a result |

Attribution and share-alike summary: the only weak-copyleft *code* obligation
is Eigen's MPL-2.0. The only share-alike *data* obligation that can attach is
ChEMBL's CC BY-SA 3.0, which today applies to identifiers only. UniProt
(CC BY 4.0) and the curl licence carry attribution obligations. Everything else
above is permissive, public domain, or executed rather than distributed.
